      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With a hand containing Necrodominance (BBB) and Sheoldred (2BB) — both powerful but slow cards — along with Thoughtseize and Fatal Push for interaction, choosing to be on the draw gives the opponent the initiative. This hand wants to deploy Necrodominance on turn 3, and being on the play would let you Thoughtseize turn 1 before the opponent can deploy threats, then land Necrodominance a full turn earlier relative to the opponent's development. Against an aggressive Izzet deck with cards like Dragon's Rage Channeler and Slickshot Show-Off, being on the draw means the opponent gets to develop first and potentially deal significant damage before Necrodominance or Sheoldred come online.",
