    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Thundering Falls tapped on turn 1 instead of Steam Vents means the player cannot cast Dragon's Rage Channeler on turn 1. DRC is one of the best possible turn 1 plays in this archetype, as it enables early surveil triggers and can become a 3/3 flyer. With Steam Vents (paying 2 life to have it enter untapped), the player could cast DRC immediately. The Thundering Falls could then be played tapped on turn 2 when the player likely wants to plot Slickshot Show-Off (which costs 1R and wouldn't be castable off just Thundering Falls + Steam Vents on turn 2 anyway since Thundering Falls only makes U/R). Actually, on turn 2 with Steam Vents (R) + Thundering Falls (R), they'd have 1R available to plot Slickshot or cast Cori-Steel Cutter. Playing Steam Vents untapped turn 1 for DRC, then Thundering Falls tapped turn 2 still gives access to 1R on turn 2 for plotting Slickshot. This is a clearly better sequence.",
      "action_taken": "Played Thundering Falls tapped on turn 1, unable to cast any spell.",
      "better_line": "Play Steam Vents untapped (pay 2 life, going to 18) and cast Dragon's Rage Channeler on turn 1. Play Thundering Falls tapped on turn 2, then have 1R available to plot Slickshot Show-Off or cast Cori-Steel Cutter.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 3,
      "player": "Gem25P Villain",
      "decision_index": 5,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "On turn 1 with no lands in play and 7 mana needed to hardcast Soul Spike, the player chose to exile two black cards from hand to pay the alternative cost. The only black cards in hand are Necrodominance, Fatal Push, Thoughtseize, and Sheoldred, the Apocalypse. Exiling any two of these is catastrophic - these are the deck's best cards. Necrodominance is the engine card, Sheoldred is the win condition, Thoughtseize is key disruption, and Fatal Push is essential removal. Spending 3 cards (Soul Spike + 2 exiled) to deal 4 damage and gain 4 life on turn 1 when the opponent has no board presence worth killing (just a tapped land) is a massive waste of resources. The opponent is at 20 life so 4 damage is minimal, and the life gain is unnecessary at 20 life. This leaves the player with only a Swamp, Undercity Sewers, and whichever two black cards remain - a devastated hand.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Soul Spike using alternative cost (exile two black cards from hand) targeting the opponent for 4 damage on turn 1.",
      "better_line": "Do not cast Soul Spike at all this turn. Play Undercity Sewers or Swamp, and develop the game plan normally with Thoughtseize on turn 1 (if playing Swamp), setting up Necrodominance on turn 3 and Sheoldred on turn 4. Soul Spike should be held for a critical moment or discarded, not cast by exiling premium cards for minimal impact.",
      "type": "blunder",
