    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Exiling Fatal Push and Thoughtseize to cast Soul Spike on turn 1 is a massive resource waste. The player is 3-for-1ing themselves (exiling Soul Spike, Fatal Push, and Thoughtseize) to deal 4 damage to the opponent at 20 life, gaining 4 life when they're also at 20. Fatal Push is premium removal in Modern, and Thoughtseize is one of the best disruption spells in the format. The player has Necrodominance and Sheoldred in hand - their game plan should be to disrupt with Thoughtseize, deploy Necrodominance on turn 3, and grind out card advantage. Instead they're throwing away their two best early interaction spells for a negligible 4 damage to face. This leaves them with no interaction against the opponent's early threats (the opponent already played a land and could have aggressive creatures like DRC or Slickshot Show-Off coming).",
      "action_taken": "Exiled Fatal Push and Thoughtseize to cast Soul Spike for free, dealing 4 damage to opponent and gaining 4 life on turn 1.",
