    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Necrodominance (BBB) in hand and Sheoldred (2BB) also in hand, the player needs black mana sources as fast as possible. Playing Undercity Sewers this turn (which enters tapped) would set it up to produce mana on turn 2, while the Swamp could be played untapped on turn 2 instead. Since the player has no 1-mana plays available this turn anyway (Fatal Push has no target), playing the tapped land now costs nothing in tempo and gets it online sooner. This sequencing matters for casting Necrodominance on turn 3 - the player needs 3 black sources by then, and Undercity Sewers produces black mana. Additionally, Undercity Sewers triggers surveil 1 on entry, which helps fill the graveyard (already has Soul Spike there). Playing the Swamp first means the Sewers must enter tapped on a later turn when the mana might be needed untapped.",
